+## 5. Reproduction appendix
+
+Analysis scripts were written to `/tmp/opencode/analyze.py` and `/tmp/opencode/analyze2.py` (not committed, ephemeral). Core method: read every snapshot with `open(f,'rb').read()`, parse JSON, compute `sha256(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in d.items() if k!='observed_at'}, sort_keys=True, separators=(',',':')).encode())` as the content-state key; aggregate status counts over `data['per_change']`; bucket bytes by UTC day of `observed_at`; compare `os.stat(f).st_mtime` to `observed_at`. The checker was executed read-only with `timeout 90 /bin/sh /var/lib/lubko/wd/viche/government/suite-compliance-check.sh /var/lib/lubko/wd/viche`, piping stdout through a JSON filter that removes `per_change`. No state, law, or production file was modified. The live root grew from 8,707 to 8,708 files during the inquiry, so the two analysis runs differ by one file and ~456 KB; all ratios are stable to <0.01%.
